-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":6240193,"digest":"sha256:eb59141c48e94bb93ab7053e9e8725012eee1749e4432e9c71804d23abbdff57","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:56:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T17:56:45Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/truss/releases/download/v0.0.51/umf_truss-0.0.51-py3-none-any.whl"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DocumentDrivenDX/truss/releases/assets/682405451","id":682405451,"node_id":"RA_kwDOUoi0Ac4orK5L","name":"umf_truss-0.0.51.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/x-gtar","state":"uploaded","size":6712731,"digest":"sha256:0f091b8c87428a003cf2a5cc68c3905fca66a3cd35e23d353b015346afd4718c","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:56:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T17:56:45Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/truss/releases/download/v0.0.51/umf_truss-0.0.51.tar.gz"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DocumentDrivenDX/truss/tarball/v0.0.51","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DocumentDrivenDX/truss/zipball/v0.0.51","body":"\n# Truss v0.0.51\n\nPublished on 2026-10-27 through the [immutable GitHub release](https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/truss/releases/tag/v0.0.51)\nand [PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/umf-truss/0.0.51/). The\n[final publication proof](../evidence/truss-0.0.51-publication/README.md)\nretains the original exact-tag Linux and Actions OIDC/public-consumer receipts.\n\n## Release scope and highlights\n\nThe Python distribution is `umf-truss==0.0.51`. The `truss` import, CLI entry\npoints and runtime protocols retain their identities. The release preserves the\nexisting PostgreSQL 18.6 runtime, embedded UMF JavaScript/V8 owners and selected\n`weft-sql==0.4.51` dependency. Existing query/disclosure source archives keep their\nexact compiler identities.\n\nPython users receive a universal wheel and source archive through GitHub and\nPyPI. Host applications continue to own authenticated connections, transactions,\nconnection pools and admission of the installed dependency cohort.\n\n## Changes and fixes\n\nRelease and OIDC publication paths select the distribution/archive name by\nversion. Historical `truss-toolkit` archives and receipts retain their original\nmeaning. New-name publication requires an actually immutable GitHub release;\nthe fresh public-index consumer checks the exact declared query dependency.\n\nThe migration index retains the exact published 0.0.50 index, SHA-256\n`4c6baf0282e3d0b5492f070c9c07d89ff0c9a819e748f3820f60b11c1f51c7aa`, and the\noriginal public 0.0.50 wheel is an existing-current fixture. Earlier immutable\nrecipes, admitted sources and native SQL remain unchanged. No physical migration\nedge or receipt is fabricated for this package rename.\n\n## Required actions\n\nUse the new distribution name in dependency declarations and retain\n`import truss`. Install in a fresh environment because the old and renamed\npackages provide the same import tree:\n\n```sh\npython -m pip install 'umf-truss[native,query]==0.0.51'\n```\n\nLocal PostgreSQL installation remains a separate optional runtime flow with its\npublished binary constraints; the host-supplied connection path does not require\nthat local-server extra.\n\n## Migration and hold guidance\n\nOnly the latest Truss application runtime is supported. Every admitted database\nlineage retains its explicit forward path to latest; old application runtimes do\nnot remain supported. Pre-0.10 UMF sources and downgrades remain unsupported.\nStartup never automatically upgrades or resets a database.\n\nThe 0.0.49/0.0.50 native tuple remains current without an artificial migration.\nOlder admitted sources use the existing explicit administrative migration flow.\nPreserve original receipts and use the latest tool to verify the target. Hold\nan application rollout when its actual installed cohort or native verification\nfails; do not rewrite retained evidence to make it appear current.\n\n## Qualification and known limits\n\n[Exact-tag Linux run 40549597103](https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/truss/actions/runs/40549597103)\npassed at normal merge/tag source `26c1b9171718ad0f6291b82f65c8cef0406886fb`:\n108 populated migration/existing-current cases, 62 HF cases, 174 managed-grant\ntests, all without skips, plus the required remaining installed workflows and\nselected small public workload. GitHub release `425804959` has 17 immutable\nassets. Automatic [Actions publisher 40555332184](https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/truss/actions/runs/40555332184)\npassed actual OIDC upload, exact public served-byte checks and a fresh\npublic-index `[query]` install importing Truss and Weft 0.4.51. Independently\ndownloaded PyPI wheel/sdist bytes equal the GitHub release assets.\n\n[Candidate Linux qualification](../evidence/truss-0.0.51-candidate-linux/README.md)\nbinds source `f3fc953814f71fe4c8e4abaa86b762a51b53add0` to 108 populated\nlineage/existing-current cases, 62 independent HF cases and 174 managed-grant\ntests, all without skips, plus the complete remaining installed native workflows\nand selected small public workload. That earlier source and its candidate\nreceipts remain distinct from the final merged/tagged source and publication\nreceipts above.\n\nThe tested native profile is Linux x86_64, Python 3.11, PostgreSQL 18.6 and the\nrecorded exact dependencies. CI runs on Linux only. The universal Truss wheel\nand selected public macOS ARM64 Weft 0.4.51 wheel remain available. Historical\nmacOS evidence retains its original versions and scope; it does not qualify\nTruss 0.0.51 installed execution or populated migrations on macOS. Managed\nLakebase acceptance and broader performance/platform claims remain separate.\n\nWeft 0.4.55 adoption is deferred until a preserving consumer-archive migration is\nqualified. Replacing compiler identities alone would strand stored 0.4.51\nquery/disclosure archives. Truss retains its exact embedded UMF JavaScript\nbundles; Core 0.10.3's Python release is not a new Truss Python dependency or\npermission to repin those bundles.\n\n## References\n\n- [Previous public 0.0.50 scope](../../04-build/releases/v0.0.50.md)\n- [Forward migration plan](../../04-build/runtime-migration-restoration-plan.md)\n- [Migration contract](../../02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-008-layout-bootstrap.md)\n- [Deployment and public distribution](../README.md)\n- [Selected public Weft 0.4.51](https://github.com/DocumentDrivenDX/weft/releases/tag/v0.4.51)\n"}